WEBVTT

00:00:03.203 --> 00:00:10.102
First the official FreeCAD 1.1.4 (the title bar says FreeCAD): a 20 mm cube, fillet all edges, radius 11

00:00:10.102 --> 00:00:22.102
The radius is more than half the edge, so this fillet cannot exist — let's see what the software says

00:00:31.356 --> 00:00:41.724
Tick “Use all edges”, radius 11, OK

00:00:41.724 --> 00:00:47.305
Official FreeCAD 1.1.4: no error, the tree looks fine — it seems to have “worked”

00:00:47.305 --> 00:00:59.305
Check it with Check geometry

00:01:01.614 --> 00:01:13.614
Check geometry: the solid is “invalid” — shell not closed, faces open, bad curves on edges; the 3D view shows the mess too. This “successful” fillet is broken, and everything built on it inherits that

00:01:19.174 --> 00:01:31.174
Same file, same steps, now in WenQuest CAD

00:01:40.314 --> 00:01:48.173
Tick “Use all edges”, radius 11, OK

00:01:48.173 --> 00:01:57.319
WenQuest CAD: an error right away — “Fillet result is not a valid solid. The size may be too large”. The broken result is never stored

00:01:57.319 --> 00:02:09.319
Change the radius to 5, OK: the fillet works
